          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Formation of the Islamic Republic</strong><br>\nAfter the Shah's government was overthrown in 1979, Khomeini returned to Iran triumphantly. He was influential in shaping the new government, advocating for an Islamic republic based on Sharia law. He argued that only a government led by religious authorities could truly represent the people and protect the country's Islamic identity.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The U.S. Embassy Hostage Crisis</strong><br>\nUnder Khomeini's leadership, Iran underwent significant changes, including the U.S. Embassy hostage crisis in 1979. Iranian students, following Khomeini's line against American interference, took 52 Americans hostage. Khomeini supported the students' actions, which led to a diplomatic standoff, further isolating Iran from the international community.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Iran-Iraq War</strong><br>\nThe Iran-Iraq War began in 1980 and lasted eight years, becoming one of the longest and most destructive conflicts of the 20th century. Khomeini's resolve shaped Iran's war efforts, often emphasizing the war as a means to resist against external oppression and to defend Islamic values.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
